From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcc45tr <mcc45tr@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 21:21:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Input: nt36523: replay touch wake after display resume

The PM core holds a wake IRQ pending until device IRQs resume. On Nabu the
display notifier may reload the touch firmware before the pending IRQ thread
can acquire the touch lock. In that case bTouchIsAwake is already true and
the original low-power gesture packet is no longer available, so the normal
gesture decoder never emits KEY_WAKEUP to the compositor.

Remember whether the IRQ thread started while the touchscreen was in
system suspend and gesture mode. If display resume won the race, report a
wake key without attempting a stale SPI read. Keep the normal packet-based
double-tap decoder for the case where the controller is still in gesture
mode. No access to suspended SPI hardware is added.

This addresses a possible lost-key race; physical Nabu DT2W validation is
still required before claiming a working wake gesture.

Signed-off-by: mcc45tr <mcc45tr@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36523/nt36xxx.c | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36523/nt36xxx.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36523/nt36xxx.c
index 393c616b5..8b7767b9c 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36523/nt36xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/nt36523/nt36xxx.c
@@ -1025,6 +1025,15 @@ static uint32_t nvt_dump_fw_history(void)
 }
 
 #define POINT_DATA_LEN 65
+static void nvt_report_wake_key(void)
+{
+	pm_wakeup_event(&ts->client->dev, 5000);
+	input_report_key(ts->input_dev, KEY_WAKEUP, 1);
+	input_sync(ts->input_dev);
+	input_report_key(ts->input_dev, KEY_WAKEUP, 0);
+	input_sync(ts->input_dev);
+}
+
 /*******************************************************
 Description:
 	Novatek touchscreen work function.
@@ -1035,6 +1044,9 @@ static uint32_t nvt_dump_fw_history(void)
 static irqreturn_t nvt_ts_work_func(int irq, void *data)
 {
 	int32_t ret = -1;
+	bool wake_irq = !READ_ONCE(bTouchIsAwake) &&
+			READ_ONCE(ts->db_wakeup) &&
+			READ_ONCE(ts->dev_pm_suspend);
 	uint8_t point_data[POINT_DATA_LEN + PEN_DATA_LEN + 1 + DUMMY_BYTES] = {0};
 	uint32_t position = 0;
 	uint32_t input_x = 0;
@@ -1072,6 +1084,17 @@ static irqreturn_t nvt_ts_work_func(int irq, void *data)
 	mutex_lock(&ts->lock);
 	if (READ_ONCE(ts->offline))
 		goto XFER_ERROR;
+	/*
+	 * A wake IRQ is held pending until the PM core re-enables device IRQs.
+	 * In the meantime the display notifier can reload firmware and mark the
+	 * touchscreen awake.  In that case the original gesture report is gone;
+	 * still deliver KEY_WAKEUP so the compositor lights the screen.
+	 */
+	if (wake_irq && bTouchIsAwake) {
+		NVT_INFO("touch wake IRQ replayed after display resume\n");
+		nvt_report_wake_key();
+		goto XFER_ERROR;
+	}
 
 	if (ts->pen_support)
 		ret = CTP_SPI_READ(ts->client, point_data, POINT_DATA_LEN + PEN_DATA_LEN + 1);
@@ -1142,11 +1165,7 @@ static irqreturn_t nvt_ts_work_func(int irq, void *data)
 			}
 
 			NVT_INFO("Gesture: double tap wakeup\n");
-			pm_wakeup_event(&ts->client->dev, 5000);
-			input_report_key(ts->input_dev, KEY_WAKEUP, 1);
-			input_sync(ts->input_dev);
-			input_report_key(ts->input_dev, KEY_WAKEUP, 0);
-			input_sync(ts->input_dev);
+			nvt_report_wake_key();
 		}
 
 		goto XFER_ERROR;
-- 
